    {
      "text": "Murkrow was feared and loathed as the alleged bearer of ill fortune. This Pokémon shows strong interest in anything that sparkles or glitters. It will even try to steal rings from women.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Murkrow was feared and loathed as the alleged bearer of ill fortune. This Pokémon shows strong interest in anything that sparkles or glitters. It will even try to steal rings from women.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "They awaken at dusk and take wing in the twilight, leading to the expression, “Get home before the Murkrow fly.”",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Seen as a symbol of bad luck, it’s generally disliked. Yet it gives presents—objects that sparkle or shine—to Trainers it’s close to.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It has a weakness for shiny things. It’s been known to sneak into the nests of Gabite—noted collectors of jewels—in search of treasure.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It searches for shiny things for its boss. Murkrow’s presence is said to be unlucky, so many people detest it.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Widely shunned as a bearer of ill fortune. Upon crossing paths with this creature, I've been told one must chant ”Workrum, Workrum—bad luck, don't come” as a protective incantation.",
      "version": "legends-arceus"
    }
